// are invented.
// - 4688: a launch that names only the creator, whose account runs the process,
// - Sysmon 1: a launch with its own user and the original file name of a
//   renamed executable,
// - Sysmon 5: a termination, which CIM cannot represent as an action,
// - 4688: a launch with explicit credentials, whose creator differs from the
//   account that runs the process,
// - security control decisions of an invented EDR, one per process name:
//   Unknown action with a Blocked disposition, an unknown outcome without
//   decision, Allowed, Denied, Observed with a successful launch, and an
//   Allowed action with a Blocked disposition.
